{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva","id":532050,"title":"Blood and Smoke Daeva","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-29T10:54:22-07:00","id":532050,"title":"Blood and Smoke Daeva","content":"I have noticed that the new Daeva attract alot of publicity, People look at them and pine for OWoD Brujah (The ones whom are passionate about their causes to a almost fevored pitch), The NWoD Daeva (Who are creatures of their Vice!).<br /> <br /> Does the new Daeva (The Penultimate hunters, who master the art of feeding as to not be affilcted by the curse) not seem enjoyable to people? To be honest, I welcome our new Aphex Predator Overlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5519-azerkatil","name":"Azerkatil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T10:59:54-07:00","id":532071,"title":"","content":"I hadn't noticed that at all. I think I've seen one post that mentioned the Brujah.<br /> <br /> People seem to like the daeva, they just think the clan weakness is a big weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:15:40-07:00","id":532082,"title":"","content":"My favorite clan is the Daeva with a Nos at close second. I think Daeva are meant to be played as you want to play them, be that special snowflake if you want, however my Daeva love life and love people. They cling to humanity and humans. They love their dolls and have embraced their weakness. So you become attached to a mortal, just make sure its a mortal you loved first and its all good. The weakness could be super harsh if you are not a lover or dont embrace the possibilty. I have had a few cruel fighter-type daeva who have bit that bullet. I am not sure if Nwod players crave the Owod Daeva instead, but it seems that the vamps in 2E arent emotionally dead like the previous ones. Disclaimer, this is just my interpretation. I could stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:20:49-07:00","id":532113,"title":"","content":"The Daeva are the scariest vampires, to me. They make you like, want and even need them. They make you want to give your blood freely - look forward to it, in fact. With a Savage at least there's the inherent honesty in the predator/prey relationship - they hunt you, you die. With the Serpents, it's all inverted because it is in their nature to turn people into willing sacrifices.<br /> <br /> It's only naturally, given their powers of controlling people's emotions and making them addicted, they cannot control their own.<br /> <br /> Yeah. They're probably my favourite clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:46:22-07:00","id":532126,"title":"","content":"You see, Daeva in VtR-1 were an amalgam of two passionate clans of VtM for me, taking the best of both: Brujah and Toreador. Their Curse was no less individual then Nosferatu's or Ventrue's, and it was COOL! Every single individual of the same clan had his own curse, in the case of Daeva taking the worst of his own personality and turning it into a burning passion. Having Vices turned into more individualistic way in God-Machine Chronicle, I could hope their curse would be more individual, but... alas, it works the same way for every Daeva. Of course, they can choose their own way to deal with it, but still too little options. And they are not PASSIONATE anymore. They're just vessel-addicted. And it's all too easy to just watch your game turning into the Twilight Saga or the 50 Shades of Red <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 05-29-2015, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:50:40-07:00","id":532139,"title":"","content":"I think my problem with this point of view is that the Brujah aren't supposed to be Daeva.<br /> <br /> They're gangrel. They're actually a gangrel bloodline and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:58:39-07:00","id":532151,"title":"","content":"nofather, well... it' not a problem. It just depends on how you see their rage. Is it feral monstrosity or rebellious passion? In the first case - Gangrel. In the second - Daeva.<br /> <br /> Really, VtM-brujah image in VtR can be expressed through any clan, and that's why I like VtR (I've been playing carthian ventrue-nazi biker, for example)...<br /> <br /> Bloodline Bruja was Gangrel bloodline, it's true. But Daeva had VtM-Brujah disciplines and their passion could be expressed in different ways, including hot-tempered rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:09:55-07:00","id":532154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva?p=532139#post532139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my problem with this point of view is that the Brujah aren't supposed to be Daeva.<br /> <br /> They're gangrel. They're actually a gangrel bloodline and everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the nWoD Gangrel and Brujah aren't related beyond being stereotypically punchy guys and the Gangrel having a bloodline called Bruja. The oWoD Brujah can very clearly be seen in the Daeva, their number one trait was passion, stereotyped as for rebellion but nobody in the Camarilla would get confused at the idea of a Brujah dedicated to maintaining order or uncovering the history of kindred political systems. This passion allowed them to draw others to them, reflected in the Presence discipline and that in early material they were the vampires most likely to be creating broods. You could say that the Brujah were the lower class version of the Toreador in some ways, but that wouldn't be doing them justice.<br /> <br /> I see the Daeva as taking after the Dark Ages high clan Brujah more than the Final Nights rebel Brujah. The 'Bruja' are a bloodline of vampire bikers, whereas the true descendents of the Brujah were the Carthians, the vampires fighting to improve kindred society instead of just relying on the tried and tested, to the point where a translated Brujah is far more likely to be a Carthian Daeva than a Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:10:44-07:00","id":532155,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of the modern Daeva weakness. The other one felt like a willpower tax that forced the awkward 7 Vice type of play if you didn't feel like paying the tax. I like the current Curse because it feels a lot more interactive, and serves as a good way for my character to have yet another strong relationship with another character.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I think inflicting the Daeva curse on someone you love (by becoming Obsessed with them) is the absolute <i>worst </i>thing you could do. (great story fodder, but not great thinking in-universe unless you as a player recognize the disastrous consequences of your actions. Could be an awesome story in fact.) It's worth pointing out that it'll only end when they're dead. There's an implication there about Daeva and the objects of their obsession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-29-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:59:34-07:00","id":532261,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that comparing Requiem Clans with Masquerade Clans was apples and oranges. That said, I do agree with Aleksay that the one of Clan Daeva's most significant defining qualities is their intense passions. But I don't agree that this is any less the case in 2e. You shouldn't need a Clan Bane forcing your character to act on their passions to have a passionate character. The Daeva haven't lost the passion aspect, the writers are just trusting you to roleplay your character without the mechanics forcing your hand. I also ADORE the new Clan Bane. I've always seen feeding as something of a metaphor for sex, or to be more accurate, intimacy. The fact that Daeva become easily addicted to the people they share that intimacy with is <i>incredibly</i> appropriate for the most passionate Clan. To top it off, the ways of coping with that tendency for addiction is even more quintessentially Daeva. They can be incredibly promiscuous feeders, never returning to the same vessel twice so they never risk get too attached, instead relying on a series of &quot;one night stand&quot; feedings. There's your &quot;Brujah&quot; interpretation right there, if you really need one. Or, they can accept that their passions are going to make them obsess over their vessels, like it or not, and pick a small number of favored vessels that they treat like a pampered harem. There's your &quot;Toreador&quot; interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T14:24:36-07:00","id":532273,"title":"","content":"I've sold Daeva as the modern version of Brujah to my group for quite sometime. Even worked with one of my players to create a Brujah bloodline for them that echoed the CWoD clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T15:03:36-07:00","id":532372,"title":"","content":"To me, the old Bruja are the Carthian movement, with the Daeva having the same discipline spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T15:28:48-07:00","id":532407,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I always thought they were sort of silly as a Clan, but their tendencies made perfect sense for a covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T15:29:38-07:00","id":532411,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Carthian Deva with a monster or rebel mask/dirge seems the best way of porting the brujah over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T01:27:40-07:00","id":542384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva?p=532372#post532372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the old Bruja are the Carthian movement, with the Daeva having the same discipline spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could tell the same for all the old word of darkness clans and bloodlines.<br /> <br /> On another note, I love the new weakness. It doesn't force roleplay like the old one, it influence it and let you play with the sexual metaphor of the vampire in a really good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T04:15:22-07:00","id":542434,"title":"","content":"I liked the old clan weakness much more than the new weakness. The clans in themselves are not that different in 2e from how I've portrayed them in the past and seeing how I got little love for two of the covenants (I've never liked the Carthian Movement or Order of the Dracul) so its mostly the weaknesses that stands out as problematic.<br /> <br /> The new weakness is just... boring. Either it warps the play so that it takes up far to much time (&quot;I need to find a new prey&quot; or &quot;I must find my prey!&quot;), or it becomes one of those &quot;meh&quot; weaknesses were you just say &quot;I drink from someone else this night&quot;. TBH I would've prefered if each clan had a set of weaknesses of which one were inheret to the character. That way, each clan would have their own weaknesses with some options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T06:24:55-07:00","id":542492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva?p=542384#post542384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you could tell the same for all the old word of darkness clans and bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div> Most of them, yes. Generally speaking, you can remake most character concepts with the right clan/covenant combination, assuming your concept didn't rely on some old power that's never been reproduced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note, I love the new weakness. It doesn't force roleplay like the old one, it influence it and let you play with the sexual metaphor of the vampire in a really good way. </div> </div> </div> I think part of the issue that some people have with the new weakness is that its so focused on the sex metaphor. With the old daeva weakness, I generally saw three Vices constantly used - Pride, Wrath, and Lust. Each produced a different feeling in the clan. The new weakness is focused on the sex that its basically cut off the vices to just Lust.<br /> <br /> I find it ironic that now the entire clan acts like suc/incubi, but we got rid of that nickname. They're more like the 'cubi than ever, but they're now called Serpents. I think its also curious that the Daeva also embody the oWoD Followers of Set attitudes now, but actually following Set is a Mehket thing, just like the Mehket swallowed Obtenebration. <br /> <br /> That said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva?p=542434#post542434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the old clan weakness much more than the new weakness. The clans in themselves are not that different in 2e from how I've portrayed them in the past and seeing how I got little love for two of the covenants (I've never liked the Carthian Movement or Order of the Dracul) so its mostly the weaknesses that stands out as problematic.<br /> <br /> The new weakness is just... boring. Either it warps the play so that it takes up far to much time (&quot;I need to find a new prey&quot; or &quot;I must find my prey!&quot;), or it becomes one of those &quot;meh&quot; weaknesses were you just say &quot;I drink from someone else this night&quot;. TBH I would've prefered if each clan had a set of weaknesses of which one were inheret to the character. That way, each clan would have their own weaknesses with some options.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do agree here. The sin-driven daeva was something that actively came up in play. Now? The clan bane doesn't come up unless we have a fair amount of feeding scenes. Or someone threatens your Herd merit. Its not nearly as evocative.<br /> <br /> I kind of feel the same way about the Mehket and Ventrue weaknesses, though. They're very easy to ignore in a lot of cases. The Gangrel curse shows up, because it means that people tread lightly around them, fearing to set off a frenzy because they have less control. Its something active that's kept in mind in all interactions. The Nossie curse... well, I've had various results with them, depending on the game, ST, and character concept, going one way or another. I've also heard some rule that Majesty's &quot;eliminate penalties&quot; clause applies to Humanity penalties, and thus effectively removing the weakness for social Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel Bane is the only one that I actually think is highly relevant to game, and the rest can be easily ignored. Clan banes this time are kind of weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:28:26-07:00","id":542777,"title":"","content":"Depends on how you approach weaknesses, I guess. If you see them as something to avoid because they hinder your character, yeah, the Clan Banes are all pretty trivial except the Gangrel one and the 1e Clan Weaknesses did a much better job of being hard to avoid and hindering your character. If you see them as something to intentionally play into because they give you another way to introduce drama into the story, then I think the 2e Clan Banes are much more evocative and tell a more interesting story than the 1e Clan Weaknesses did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-06-2015, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T13:46:36-07:00","id":542959,"title":"","content":"On the contrary, the problem is that I DON'T want to avoid them. I want them to come up in play. I want them to have an effect on my character's personality and how I play. I want them to encourage drama. The problem is... they don't. My complaint is that I don't feel they aren't evocative, that they're kind of just background noise. In the case of the Daeva (and only the Daeva), I felt the 1e bane was more interesting and evocative than the 2e bane. It came up in play fairly regularly, it had a broad effect.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in 2e, most of the banes feel like just.. random background noise. They have no bite. A Nossie socialite as a concept won't even feel the bane. On an average session, how often will the bond to the herd matter for a Daeva? Most games I've been in don't spend a notable amount of time involving herds as more than just something in the background, often off screen.<br /> <br /> Ventrue are supposed to have trouble with Touchstones, and thus be more detached, but its not really a big deal - in practice, I find that means you get a &quot;find new touchstone&quot; plot earlier than others, but that's it. Nothing that every other vampire won't experience at some point. Its really nothing that differentiates the Ven from anyone else. Hells, in some cases where other clan PCs lose Humanity faster, the Ven can keep his Touchstone longer than others! I've seen it happen. There's no &quot;interesting story&quot; here. Its the same one everyone else gets.<br /> <br /> For Mehket... same as above. Its nothing that every other vampire won't touch on at some point. Same story - if a story at all. Grave Soil isn't exactly evocative as a story element when you keep it in your haven out of sight.<br /> <br /> I just flat out disagree that the 2e clan banes are evocative. And that's a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:33:06-07:00","id":542986,"title":"","content":"I can see the point on the fluff of the old Daeva weakness, but I really can't get on board with the mechanics of it, since it just wound up as a Willpower tax. Is there any way to attain the same feel without resorting to that awkwardness, especially absent virtue &amp; vice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:45:44-07:00","id":543002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva?p=542986#post542986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the point on the fluff of the old Daeva weakness, but I really can't get on board with the mechanics of it, since it just wound up as a Willpower tax. Is there any way to attain the same feel without resorting to that awkwardness, especially absent virtue &amp; vice?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is prescedent for 2e supernats gaining a Virtue and/or Vice in addition to their gameline-specific Anchors (i.e. the Code of Honor Merit in the W:tF core). If you wanted to emulate the 1E Daeva weakness, you could just have their Bane saddle them with a Vice the first time they drop to Humanity 6, and any time they have an opportunity to act on that Vice, they either have to indulge, succeed on a Humanity roll, or gain the Deprived condition.<br /> <br /> On the subject of comparisons to Masquerade, that's also pretty much the Ravnos weakness, minus the unfortunate implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T05:27:00-07:00","id":545059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva?p=542492#post542492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree here. The sin-driven daeva was something that actively came up in play. Now? The clan bane doesn't come up unless we have a fair amount of feeding scenes. Or someone threatens your Herd merit. Its not nearly as evocative.<br /> <br /> I kind of feel the same way about the Mehket and Ventrue weaknesses, though. They're very easy to ignore in a lot of cases. The Gangrel curse shows up, because it means that people tread lightly around them, fearing to set off a frenzy because they have less control. Its something active that's kept in mind in all interactions. The Nossie curse... well, I've had various results with them, depending on the game, ST, and character concept, going one way or another. I've also heard some rule that Majesty's &quot;eliminate penalties&quot; clause applies to Humanity penalties, and thus effectively removing the weakness for social Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel Bane is the only one that I actually think is highly relevant to game, and the rest can be easily ignored. Clan banes this time are kind of weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with the Mekhet Bane is that it's generic, with it being 'take a bane, any bane. Oh, and sunlight' because I stop the 'clown doctor wielding a parakeet' problem (taking overly specific banes). The Gangrel and Nosferatu Banes RAW have no work around (the Nosferatu Bane is not a penalty but a lowered cap and it's not based on the character's actions or appearance, so RAW Majesty 1 does nothing to it), while the Daeva Bane relies on the ST making it work, so I'd go for something else (being unable to regain Willpower from their Mask unless it would also be refilled from [chosen vice], the 1e weakness, the masquerade Toreador weakness). The Ventrue weakness is the most trivial of the lot, being worth one merit point to get a humanity 6 touchstone and the fact that unless a player does not understand the themes of the game they are unlikely to reach Humanity 1, the only point where the Bane has real bite (because no even the most dedicated Ventrue can have a Humanity 1 touchstone). In my view most vampires would have two or three touchstones anyway, so the curse really loses it's bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:13:25-07:00","id":545200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/532050-blood-and-smoke-daeva?p=545059#post545059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Gangrel and Nosferatu Banes RAW have no work around (the Nosferatu Bane is not a penalty but a lowered cap and it's not based on the character's actions or appearance, so RAW Majesty 1 does nothing to it),</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm.... I think you're getting confused with some of the 1e rules here. There is no more humanity cap - lower humanity now inflicts social penalties. A -1 penalty for humanity 5-6, a -2 at 4, a -3 at 3, -5 at 2, chance die at 1. Given that its just a social penalty, and Majesty specifically removes social penalties... well, its up to individual STs, but it does seems to work. Even if not, for a large number of Nosferatu, its just a small die penalty over everyone else until Humanity 3, offset by buying up the skills or attributes.<br /> <br /> I guess that's really the problem I have. Most of them don't come up into play with the levels of humanity we're talking about. I haven't really dropped that low in Humanity in my new games yet where it matters - playing a LetS game where we're not dropping below Humanity 5 might have something to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:20:13-07:00","id":545215,"title":"","content":"My group has two Daeva, one Invictus and one Ordo, and they're both still at Humanity 7 after three stories/quests.<br /> <br /> I run a solo-game, too, where there was only one Humanity drop after three stories.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'm being overly permissive, either, because I really want to see the banes and I giggle with glee on the once-in-a-dozen sessions where they roll it.<br /> <br /> I really think Humanity doesn't drop very fast at all in 2e, though I suspect it drops faster the lower you go. My PCs just never hit the sins, or anything I'd consider a sin based on the book's guidelines. They aren't even particularly virtuous. They just aren't sociopaths.<br /> <br /> In that sense, &quot;this bane seems to never come up compared to the rest&quot; seems like less of an issue to me than &quot;no bane seems to ever come up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, my experiences may also be abnormal and biased, but they're my experiences for what they're worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T09:12:31-07:00","id":545383,"title":"","content":"I've noticed the drop becoming harder too. The diablerists in my vampire game never dropped below 4, and I was double checking them for murder and diablerie until they took a bane. And it was after several acts of diablerie and frenzies. My own werewolf hasn't dropped from his starting Harmony, despite making many penalized rolls.<br /> <br /> It might be on purpose. Since the cost of Humanity has been lowered a lot, it's possible the mechanics for loss were designed so that it was harder to happen to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:31:20-07:00","id":545508,"title":"","content":"Isn't the drop from Diablerie automatic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:33:26-07:00","id":545510,"title":"","content":"It's always a breaking point, not always Humanity loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:16:23-07:00","id":545944,"title":"","content":"Having touchstones does make Detachment rolls significantly less painful, but remember that just being forced to make the roll causes a condition unless you get an exceptional success; those conditions can really hurt under the right circumstances. A Humanity 7 vampire with two touchstones isn't likely to lose a Humanity for taking a bullet in the shoulder (Detachment roll at 7 dice for suffering an injury that would hospitalize a human), but if they get less than 5 successes they might suffer Bestial condition, making Frenzy all the more likely if the fighting continues.<br /> <br /> I think it's also important emphasize that a vampire has to work to hold on to his or her Touchstones. They represent relationships that require time and energy to maintain and secret vulnerabilities the character's enemies would love to exploit.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't get extra dice on Detachment rolls just because you know that you have a daughter out there somewhere; you have to sneak into her room at night every so often to read her a bedtime story, or dedicate time to patrolling her neighborhood and scaring the monsters and burglars away, or something similar. Likewise, you shouldn't be safe from humanity loss just because your childhood home is still standing. You have to take time to walk in the yard, look in the windows, maybe even sit by the spot where your bed used to be and have a bit of a cry. These are things that aren't necessarily easy to conceal, and which could lead to all sorts of complications, some of which might even trigger breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-08-2015, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}